content.text:
On the products page, the "All products" and "Bundles" headings are now in capitals, 16px, with 0.08em letter spacing.

I added one rule at the end of `site/css/pages.css`:

```css
.page-products .section-title {
  font-size: 16px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
}
```

- **Only the products page changes.** Four other pages use the same heading style, so the rule applies only inside the products page's `<body class="page-products">`.
- **It holds on phones too.** The rule overrides the smaller 21px size headings normally get on phones, so they stay 16px there.
- **Tests:** all functional tests pass, and so do the visual tests for every other page. The products page fails its visual comparison at desktop and phone size. I looked at the desktop difference image, and it's just the headings getting smaller and everything below moving up a few pixels to fill the space. Nothing else changed.

I haven't updated the approved screenshots. Once you're happy with the look, refresh them with `npx playwright test tests/visual.spec.ts --update-snapshots`.

STATUS: DONE

